  "applies_to": "Desert Aire SelectAire Plus (SP) indoor pool dehumidifiers running controller program version 1.x.x.",
  "summary": "SelectAire Plus units are large indoor pool dehumidifiers. The BACnet list is fixed: analog inputs for refrigerant, air, pool water and pressure sensors, four writable setpoints (space RH, space air, pool 1 and pool 2 water), binary inputs for component status and alarms, and seven writable binary values for occupancy, event, max outdoor air, purge, unit off, roof lockout and reset. A multistate input reports the unit's operating state.",
  "bacnet_transport": [],
  "firmware": "Program version 1.x.x",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "The list covers options a given unit may not have (second pool, cooling towers, VOC sensor, circuit B); those points won't carry real data.",
    "Temperature and pressure ranges are given in both imperial and metric units; check which units the controller reports.",
    "BI 48 Remote Off is 0 when the unit is off and 1 in normal operation.",
    "The source does not say whether the unit uses BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP.",
    "Instances run 1-110 continuously across object types (no two objects share an instance)."
  ],
